A||N||7||davidcwhite||88 GT backfires off of idle||||9||
Z||000000||davidcwhite||08-15-2000||06:44 PM||||I have owned my 88 GT now for about 6 months. When starting it runs rough for about 5 minutes before it really starts to warm up.  During this time while under acceleration there is an intermittent small little backfire.  It's not consistent because I never know when it's going to happen.<P>All electrical has been replaced (cap, rotor, and plugs).  The plug wires appear to be original and show no signs of discharge. I'm getting really shitty mileage (about 15mpg) but the car runs and idles fine.  After warming up (at least ten minutes) it runs much better but still will backfire while under acceleration.<P>Also the car doesn't seem to rev up very well between idle and 3,000 rpm.  It feels lumpy and uneven.  <P>Any help would be appreciated.||||reg||9
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-15-2000||06:57 PM||||It sounds like the timing could be off.  Get a timing light and check it out.<P>Another possibility is the catalytic convertor is fouled.  When they go they can plug up the exhaust flow and cause crappy performance and mileage.  <P>The cat on my very first Fiero (an '88 GT back in 1990) plugged up at 25K miles and I couldn't go faster than 20 MPH!<P>Where are you located?<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 08-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||davidcwhite||08-15-2000||07:09 PM||||The cat was replaced a few months ago.  I checked and reset the timing at least 3 times.  ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Phil||08-15-2000||07:30 PM||||Just have to ask. You did ground out the ECM for timing right?||||reg||1
Z||000004||davidcwhite||08-16-2000||10:45 AM||||Yes it was grounded out.  Replaced the plug wires last night but still no change.  When I first start up the car in the morning and drive off to work it sounds like its not running on all cylinders.  After it gets past 3000 rpm I can feel it kick into all the cylinders.  It only does this when it's cold. After it warms up its fine. <P>It's got to be something to do with the fuel injection!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000005||Mark||08-16-2000||09:45 PM||||David, sounds like ignition to me.  I would check and double check the firing order of the plug wires.  Also, do you get a nice blue spark? (To check for spark, pull one wire and connect it to a spare spark plug.  Ground the plug with a test lead, start car and take a look.)  You may also have a bad plug.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pretender||08-17-2000||03:02 AM||||It could also be your fuel pump. i'm having the exact same problem now. on my 88gt. i've been meaning to upgrade the fuel pump because of my nitrous, so might as well upgrade. ||||reg||10
Z||000007||davidcwhite||08-17-2000||10:43 AM||||Success!!!<BR>The Chilton manual says to disconnect the 4 prong lead into the distributor before setting the timing.  This is not the same thing as resetting the ECM into diagnostic mode.  In fact I read and re-read the procedures in the manual and found almost nothing about resetting the ECM into diagnostic mode.  Once that was done the timning was way off, hence the backfiring.<BR>It's like I have a new car.<P>Thanks for everyone's helps and suggestions.<P>PS  Why in the world is the best forum for Fiero in the Netherlands?||||reg||6
